module lib/hf/hf
  The Hartree-Fock pipeline as the verification layer runs it. lib/hf/scf
  computes each stage by its production member (`integrals(mol, o)`, then
  `scf(setup)`); here, with `cross_check` on (`scf_checked()`), every
  integral stage runs each of its methods (lib/hf/integrals) and asserts
  that they agree, and with it off each def hands over to the production
  one. The input is a `Molecule` (lib/hf/molecule) and an `ScfOptions`
  record (lib/hf/opts); the output is an `ScfResult` (lib/hf/scf_loop).

  The lock helpers at the end hold a molecule against PySCF's stored
  integrals and energies; the lock ladder (scf/lock_*.viv) calls them.

hf_eri  @f0774fb2
  why   The repulsion integrals are the costly stage: `n^4/8` distinct
        numbers. Packing them by the eight-fold symmetry of `(ij|kl)` keeps
        one copy of each.
  mol   the molecule: atoms, shells and primitives
  o     the run's options: `cross_check`, and the member mask it uses
  rep   the sweep's report
  G     the packed repulsion integrals over Cartesian functions: `(ij|kl)` is
        the Coulomb repulsion between the charge distributions `i j` and `k l`
  m     the transform members to run: all that apply to the shells, or the
        production one alone
  ns    the number of spherical functions
  G5    the packed repulsion integrals over spherical functions

  compute        compute the integrals over Cartesian functions, comparing the methods in the mask
  if the run is spherical
    transform      transform all four indices to spherical functions
  return the packed integrals

hf_setup  @a037c134
  mol   the molecule
  o     the run's options
  S     the overlap matrix in the run's functions, `[n, n]`
  H     the core Hamiltonian in the run's functions, `[n, n]`
  G     what the J/K stage reads: the packed repulsion integrals, or the
        basis blob for a direct run

  one_electron   compute the overlap S and the one-electron Hamiltonian H
  two_electron   compute the electron repulsion integrals, or the basis description for a direct build
  return the setup

hf_energy  @8a9e2ae3
  why   Water STO-3G gives PySCF's energy
        [test "water STO-3G from the packs: RHF, and UHF on the closed shell, give PySCF's energy"],
        and so does water 6-31G* in spherical functions
        [test "water 6-31G* in 5D from the packs gives PySCF's spherical energy"].
  mol   the molecule
  o     the run's options
  p     the setup: every integral and the electron counts
  r     the SCF's result: energy, orbitals, densities, convergence record

  integrals      build the setup: every integral and the electron counts
  scf            solve the Hartree-Fock equations with them
  return the result

hf_gap  @bcfc79ae
  what  The largest difference between two arrays over their first N
        entries, in row-major order.
  A     one array
  B     the other array, the same length or longer
  N     how many entries, in row-major order, to compare
  ix    the flat indexes `0..N-1`
  a     A's first N entries
  b     B's first N entries
  w     the largest gap seen so far
  i     the entry being compared

hf_eri_oracle  @51b5bfd0
  what  Compare packed repulsion integrals with a sampled reference, for a
        basis too large to store every integral: the worst sampled gap, the
        worst gap on the pair diagonal, and the relative gaps of two
        checksums.
  why   PySCF's full list of integrals for a larger basis is too big to
        store in the repository; sampled entries, the pair diagonal and two
        checksums catch a wrong integral without it.
  G      the packed repulsion integrals to check
  idx    the packed indexes of the sampled entries
  val    PySCF's values at those indexes
  diag   PySCF's pair-diagonal values `(ij|ij)`
  sumsq  PySCF's sum of squares of every integral
  wsum   PySCF's seeded weighted sum of every integral
  seed   the seed of the weights of that sum
  worst  the largest gap on the pair diagonal so far
  p      a pair index on the diagonal
  cs     the two checksums of G

hf_lock_report  @80cede00
  why   A converged density that one more plain step leaves in place is a
        true fixed point, not a run that stopped early.
  p     the setup to run
  eref  PySCF's energy for it, hartree
  r     the converged result
  f     the result of one plain step from r's densities

  scf            run the SCF
  fixed          take one plain step from the result and measure how far it moves
  return the report

hf_lock_assert  @f56e0821
  why   The commutator is held for RHF and UHF only: at a converged ROHF
        state the spin Fock matrices do not commute with their densities.
  r     the lock report
  p     the setup it came from, for the method

hf_oracle_assert  @89035d67
  what  Assert a sampled-oracle report: every entry within `1e-12`.
  g     the report `hf_eri_oracle` returns

